      "body": "`peers` is populated symmetrically for each coactive pair (both `a -> b` and `b -> a`), but this loop canonicalizes `(src,dst)` and pushes an edge for both directions, creating duplicate neighbor edges that then have to be sorted and deduped later. Emitting the neighbor edge only once (e.g., only when `a < b`) avoids extra allocations and sort/dedup work while keeping the same canonical output.",
